1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,167
Welcome to WorkPulse.

2
00:00:01,217 --> 00:00:02,385
Track, focus, achieve.

3
00:00:02,435 --> 00:00:08,472
In this tutorial you will learn how to use
WorkPulse from beginning to end: setting

4
00:00:08,522 --> 00:00:13,341
up your organization, inviting your team,
tracking time with the desktop app,

5
00:00:13,391 --> 00:00:17,399
approving timesheets, billing your
clients, running payroll, and getting the

6
00:00:17,449 --> 00:00:18,617
reports you need.

7
00:00:18,667 --> 00:00:23,486
Everything you see is the real
application, running with a demo company

8
00:00:23,536 --> 00:00:27,950
called Northwind Creative, so you can
follow along step by step.

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,362
WorkPulse has three kinds of users.

10
00:00:32,412 --> 00:00:37,185
Administrators and managers use this web
app to organize people and projects,

11
00:00:37,235 --> 00:00:39,999
approve time, and handle billing and
payroll.

12
00:00:40,049 --> 00:00:45,626
Workers, the people whose time is tracked,
use the WorkPulse desktop app on Windows,

13
00:00:45,676 --> 00:00:46,832
macOS or Linux.

14
00:00:46,882 --> 00:00:52,862
It tracks their time and shows them their
own timesheet, time off and pay stubs.

15
00:00:52,912 --> 00:00:58,891
And your clients can get a read-only
client portal that shows the work done for

16
00:00:58,941 --> 00:01:00,499
them, without any money.

17
00:01:00,549 --> 00:01:06,126
What each person sees depends on their
role, so two people can see different

18
00:01:06,176 --> 00:01:06,528
menus.

19
00:01:06,578 --> 00:01:10,950
That is normal, and we will come back to
it later.

20
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:17,750
The menu on the left follows the way work
flows through WorkPulse.

21
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:20,950
You set up the organization and invite
people.

22
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,550
You organize the work into clients,
projects and tasks.

23
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:26,150
Your team tracks time.

24
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:28,150
Managers review and approve it.

25
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:30,550
Approved time becomes invoices and
payroll.

26
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:33,350
And reports turn it all into insight.

27
00:01:33,400 --> 00:01:38,950
This tutorial follows the same order, and
the chapter list in the description lets

28
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:40,950
you jump to any part.

29
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,804
To start using WorkPulse, create your
organization.

30
00:01:48,854 --> 00:01:55,736
Enter your name, the name of your company,
your work email and a password of at least

31
00:01:55,786 --> 00:01:56,552
ten characters.

32
00:01:56,602 --> 00:01:58,183
Then click Create organization.

33
00:01:58,233 --> 00:02:03,076
You are the owner of this new
organization, and WorkPulse takes you

34
00:02:03,126 --> 00:02:04,707
straight to the Overview.

35
00:02:04,757 --> 00:02:10,008
For a new organization, the Overview shows
a Getting started checklist with five

36
00:02:10,058 --> 00:02:15,717
steps: invite your team, create a project,
set pay and bill rates, connect the

37
00:02:15,767 --> 00:02:18,571
desktop app, and review what is tracked.

38
00:02:18,621 --> 00:02:24,688
Each step links to the right page, and it
ticks itself off as you go.

39
00:02:24,738 --> 00:02:27,950
You can hide the checklist at any time.

40
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:33,593
Next time, sign in from the Welcome Back
page.

41
00:02:33,643 --> 00:02:39,260
If you forget your password, click Forgot
password, enter your work email and click

42
00:02:39,310 --> 00:02:40,474
Send reset link.

43
00:02:40,524 --> 00:02:44,521
WorkPulse emails you a link to choose a
new password.

44
00:02:44,571 --> 00:02:50,998
For your privacy, the message is the same
whether or not the address has an account.

45
00:02:51,048 --> 00:02:55,045
Back on the sign-in page, enter your email
and password.

46
00:02:55,095 --> 00:02:59,498
The eye button shows the password so you
can check it.

47
00:02:59,548 --> 00:03:03,950
Click Sign in, and WorkPulse opens the
organization you used last.

48
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:10,479
When someone invites you to their
organization, you receive an invitation

49
00:03:10,529 --> 00:03:10,891
link.

50
00:03:10,941 --> 00:03:12,950
Opening it shows this page.

51
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:17,068
Check your name, choose a password and
click Join organization.

52
00:03:17,118 --> 00:03:21,597
Managers and administrators land in the
web app, ready to work.

53
00:03:21,647 --> 00:03:27,362
Workers are taken to a page where they
download the desktop app instead, because

54
00:03:27,412 --> 00:03:30,244
that is where they track their time.

55
00:03:30,294 --> 00:03:33,950
You will see that page in the desktop
chapter.

56
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,382
Protect your account with two-factor
sign-in.

57
00:03:38,432 --> 00:03:42,842
Open the account menu, choose Profile and
devices, and find Two-factor

58
00:03:42,892 --> 00:03:43,247
authentication.

59
00:03:43,297 --> 00:03:46,085
Click Set up and confirm your password.

60
00:03:46,135 --> 00:03:51,761
Scan the QR code with an authenticator app
on your phone, such as Google

61
00:03:51,811 --> 00:03:56,626
Authenticator or Microsoft Authenticator,
then type the six-digit code it shows and

62
00:03:56,676 --> 00:03:57,842
click Turn on.

63
00:03:57,892 --> 00:04:00,680
WorkPulse now gives you ten recovery
codes.

64
00:04:00,730 --> 00:04:04,734
Each one works once, if you ever lose your
phone.

65
00:04:04,784 --> 00:04:10,004
Download them and keep them somewhere
safe, tick the box and click Done.

66
00:04:10,054 --> 00:04:14,869
From now on, signing in asks for a code
from your phone.

67
00:04:14,919 --> 00:04:20,139
Administrators can also require two-factor
for everyone, which we will see in the

68
00:04:20,189 --> 00:04:20,950
security chapter.

69
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,397
The Overview is your home page.

70
00:04:28,447 --> 00:04:32,474
It updates live, so you always see the
current picture.

71
00:04:32,524 --> 00:04:38,183
At the top, This month shows the time
logged, the estimated pay, the billable

72
00:04:38,233 --> 00:04:41,037
time and the estimated amount to bill.

73
00:04:41,087 --> 00:04:46,338
Estimates come from your rates and become
final once the time is approved.

74
00:04:46,388 --> 00:04:51,232
Worked today shows how much your team has
tracked so far today.

75
00:04:51,282 --> 00:04:56,533
Waiting for approval counts the timesheets
and manual time requests that need your

76
00:04:56,583 --> 00:05:01,018
decision, and Project budgets warns you
before a project runs over.

77
00:05:01,068 --> 00:05:06,727
The switch at the top right changes whose
numbers you see: everyone, only yourself,

78
00:05:06,777 --> 00:05:07,950
or one member.

79
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:14,399
You can arrange the Overview to suit the
way you work.

80
00:05:14,449 --> 00:05:15,208
Click Customize.

81
00:05:15,258 --> 00:05:22,085
Every card now has controls to change its
size, move it up or down, or hide it.

82
00:05:22,135 --> 00:05:28,557
Hidden cards wait in the Hidden widgets
panel, so you can add them back at any

83
00:05:28,607 --> 00:05:28,961
time.

84
00:05:29,011 --> 00:05:34,624
There are cards for the current timer, who
is working, recent screenshots, time off,

85
00:05:34,674 --> 00:05:37,051
attendance, invoices, weekly limits and
more.

86
00:05:37,101 --> 00:05:41,096
When you are happy with the layout, click
Save layout.

87
00:05:41,146 --> 00:05:45,950
Each person has their own layout, and
Reset brings back the default.

88
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:52,774
The sidebar groups the pages by job: Time
Tracking, Workforce, Project Management,

89
00:05:52,824 --> 00:05:56,793
Finance and Reports, with Settings and
Help at the bottom.

90
00:05:56,843 --> 00:05:59,205
Click a group to open it.

91
00:05:59,255 --> 00:06:02,421
At the top left is the organization
switcher.

92
00:06:02,471 --> 00:06:07,646
If you belong to more than one
organization, switch between them here, or

93
00:06:07,696 --> 00:06:09,254
create a new one.

94
00:06:09,304 --> 00:06:14,881
At the top right, the bell shows your
notifications, such as a timesheet waiting

95
00:06:14,931 --> 00:06:17,695
for approval or a time off request.

96
00:06:17,745 --> 00:06:20,509
Click Mark all read to clear them.

97
00:06:20,559 --> 00:06:26,538
Next to it is your account menu, with your
profile and devices, what is monitored,

98
00:06:26,588 --> 00:06:28,950
and the light and dark themes.

99
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:33,374
Whenever you are unsure, open Help.

100
00:06:33,424 --> 00:06:37,819
The Help Center is a plain-language manual
for the whole app.

101
00:06:37,869 --> 00:06:43,475
Search for what you want to do, for
example invoice, and open a guide.

102
00:06:43,525 --> 00:06:49,132
Each guide gives you numbered steps, with
buttons that take you straight to the

103
00:06:49,182 --> 00:06:49,940
right page.

104
00:06:49,990 --> 00:06:54,384
Many pages also have their own Help link
at the top.

105
00:06:54,434 --> 00:06:57,617
If you are new, click Start the tour.

106
00:06:57,667 --> 00:07:02,061
It highlights each part of the screen with
a short explanation.

107
00:07:02,111 --> 00:07:06,506
Use Next to move on, or Skip tour to close
it.

108
00:07:06,556 --> 00:07:10,950
The tour starts by itself the first time
you sign in.

109
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:18,822
Now let us set up the organization.

110
00:07:18,872 --> 00:07:19,642
Open Settings.

111
00:07:19,692 --> 00:07:25,796
The tabs across the top hold every
setting, and you only see the ones your

112
00:07:25,846 --> 00:07:26,617
role allows.

113
00:07:26,667 --> 00:07:32,771
On the Organization tab, the General panel
sets your company name, time zone, the day

114
00:07:32,821 --> 00:07:36,873
your week starts, your currency, and how
durations are shown.

115
00:07:36,923 --> 00:07:42,206
The Company profile below holds your logo,
tax ID, address and contact details.

116
00:07:42,256 --> 00:07:45,488
They appear on your invoices and pay
stubs.

117
00:07:45,538 --> 00:07:47,950
After a change, click Save changes.

118
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:53,950
The Time and pay tab controls how time
becomes pay.

119
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:58,750
The timesheet period sets how often
members submit their time, for example

120
00:07:58,800 --> 00:07:59,550
every week.

121
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:05,550
Timesheet rules can lock old time so it
cannot be changed, set minimum hours, and

122
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:07,550
remind people about missing time.

123
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:13,550
Below are the overtime rules and your time
types, such as regular or overtime, each

124
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:16,350
with its own pay and bill multiplier.

125
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:19,950
Break types define the breaks your people
can take.

126
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:27,150
Let us add a coffee break: name it Coffee,
make it a paid break, with a maximum of

127
00:08:27,200 --> 00:08:27,950
fifteen minutes.

128
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:31,550
And a lunch break: unpaid, up to sixty
minutes.

129
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:35,950
We will plan these breaks on a project in
a moment.

130
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:41,209
Tracking policies decide what the desktop
app records.

131
00:08:41,259 --> 00:08:43,654
The organization default applies to
everyone.

132
00:08:43,704 --> 00:08:47,728
Activity counts keyboard and mouse use,
never the keys themselves.

133
00:08:47,778 --> 00:08:53,024
Idle detection asks people what to do with
time when they step away.

134
00:08:53,074 --> 00:08:59,135
Screenshots can be switched on, taken a
set number of times every ten minutes, and

135
00:08:59,185 --> 00:08:59,543
blurred.

136
00:08:59,593 --> 00:09:03,617
Apps and URLs record which applications
and websites are used.

137
00:09:03,667 --> 00:09:08,506
You can override any setting for a team or
for one member.

138
00:09:08,556 --> 00:09:12,172
Here, the Client Success team has its
screenshots blurred.

139
00:09:12,222 --> 00:09:15,024
An overridden setting shows Reset to
inherited.

140
00:09:15,074 --> 00:09:20,728
When you save, the affected members are
notified, and each member can always see

141
00:09:20,778 --> 00:09:21,950
what is monitored.

142
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:27,150
Roles control who can see and do what.

143
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:31,950
WorkPulse comes with built-in roles:
System Admin for full access, Team Manager

144
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:37,550
for running teams and projects without the
money settings, and Worker for people who

145
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:38,350
track time.

146
00:09:38,400 --> 00:09:41,550
The matrix shows every permission for
every role.

147
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:45,550
If you need something in between, create a
custom role.

148
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:51,150
Give it a name, start from an existing
role, and then adjust its permissions.

149
00:09:51,200 --> 00:09:55,950
Each permission can apply to the person
themselves, their assigned projects, their

150
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:57,950
team, or the whole organization.

151
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:07,375
To add people, open Workforce, then
Members, and click Invite member.

152
00:10:07,425 --> 00:10:11,398
Enter their email address and name, and
choose a role.

153
00:10:11,448 --> 00:10:13,812
Most people you track are Workers.

154
00:10:13,862 --> 00:10:20,249
You can also put them in teams and give
them projects right away, so everything is

155
00:10:20,299 --> 00:10:21,858
ready when they join.

156
00:10:21,908 --> 00:10:23,065
Click Send invitation.

157
00:10:23,115 --> 00:10:24,674
WorkPulse emails the invitation.

158
00:10:24,724 --> 00:10:31,111
If the email cannot be sent, the dialog
shows the invitation link so you can share

159
00:10:31,161 --> 00:10:31,916
it yourself.

160
00:10:31,966 --> 00:10:36,743
Until the person accepts, the invitation
waits under Pending invitations, where you

161
00:10:36,793 --> 00:10:37,950
can revoke it.

162
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:42,769
Click a member to open their profile.

163
00:10:42,819 --> 00:10:46,394
The Overview shows their details, quick
links and access.

164
00:10:46,444 --> 00:10:52,033
Here you can suspend or remove someone, or
reset their two-factor sign-in if they

165
00:10:52,083 --> 00:10:53,242
lose their phone.

166
00:10:53,292 --> 00:10:56,464
Personal info holds HR details and private
notes.

167
00:10:56,514 --> 00:11:01,297
The other tabs show the member's time,
activity, projects, the computers they

168
00:11:01,347 --> 00:11:06,533
use, and the tracking policy that applies
to them, combined from the organization,

169
00:11:06,583 --> 00:11:08,950
their team and any personal overrides.

170
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:13,382
Teams group people who work together.

171
00:11:13,432 --> 00:11:20,274
On the Teams tab, click New team, give it
a name and a description, and click Create

172
00:11:20,324 --> 00:11:20,680
team.

173
00:11:20,730 --> 00:11:21,896
Then add people.

174
00:11:21,946 --> 00:11:27,166
A team member with the Manager role
approves the team's timesheets and time

175
00:11:27,216 --> 00:11:30,409
off, and sees the team's time and
activity.

176
00:11:30,459 --> 00:11:36,491
Here, Priya becomes the manager of the new
Video Production team, and Kenji joins as

177
00:11:36,541 --> 00:11:37,301
a member.

178
00:11:37,351 --> 00:11:40,950
A person can belong to more than one team.

179
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:49,950
Work in WorkPulse is organized into
clients, projects and tasks.

180
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:51,550
Start with the client.

181
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:55,150
Open Project Management, then Clients, and
click New client.

182
00:11:55,200 --> 00:11:58,350
Enter the company name and a contact
person.

183
00:11:58,400 --> 00:12:01,550
The contact email is where invoices are
sent.

184
00:12:01,600 --> 00:12:07,150
Choose the client's currency, and if you
charge this client a standard hourly rate,

185
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:08,350
enter it here.

186
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:14,750
You can also add a logo, a colour and the
language for documents such as invoices.

187
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:15,950
Click Create client.

188
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:21,971
Sometimes a client is created by mistake,
for example twice.

189
00:12:22,021 --> 00:12:25,589
A client that was never used can be
deleted.

190
00:12:25,639 --> 00:12:28,404
Open its actions menu and choose Delete.

191
00:12:28,454 --> 00:12:33,228
WorkPulse explains what will be removed:
the client with its projects, tasks,

192
00:12:33,278 --> 00:12:35,239
rates, budgets and portal access.

193
00:12:35,289 --> 00:12:40,465
Deleting only works for a client with no
invoices, payments, expenses or tracked

194
00:12:40,515 --> 00:12:42,878
time, and it cannot be undone.

195
00:12:42,928 --> 00:12:46,898
For a client you have worked with, use
Archive instead.

196
00:12:46,948 --> 00:12:52,125
Archiving hides the client and its
projects but keeps all its history, and

197
00:12:52,175 --> 00:12:54,136
you can restore it later.

198
00:12:54,186 --> 00:12:56,950
Tick Show archived to see archived
clients.

199
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:04,275
Clients can follow the work you do for
them in a client portal.

200
00:13:04,325 --> 00:13:07,143
From the client's actions, open Client
portal.

201
00:13:07,193 --> 00:13:13,287
Switch the portal on and choose what the
client sees: hours per person, task and

202
00:13:13,337 --> 00:13:17,793
day, task progress and hour budgets,
activity levels, and even screenshots

203
00:13:17,843 --> 00:13:19,432
taken on their projects.

204
00:13:19,482 --> 00:13:21,480
The portal never shows money.

205
00:13:21,530 --> 00:13:25,986
Click Preview as client to see exactly
what they will see.

206
00:13:26,036 --> 00:13:30,083
To give someone access, enter their email
and click Invite.

207
00:13:30,133 --> 00:13:32,950
You can revoke access at any time.

208
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:37,799
Next, create a project for the client.

209
00:13:37,849 --> 00:13:40,241
Open Projects and click New project.

210
00:13:40,291 --> 00:13:43,497
Give it a name and choose the client.

211
00:13:43,547 --> 00:13:50,008
Add start and end dates and an estimate of
the hours, so WorkPulse can show progress

212
00:13:50,058 --> 00:13:51,229
against the plan.

213
00:13:51,279 --> 00:13:56,113
Then choose who works on it, either
individual members or whole teams.

214
00:13:56,163 --> 00:14:00,590
Members only see and track the projects
they are assigned to.

215
00:14:00,640 --> 00:14:07,915
In the finance section you can set pay and
bill rates for this project, or mark it as

216
00:14:07,965 --> 00:14:08,729
not billable.

217
00:14:08,779 --> 00:14:09,950
Click Create project.

218
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:16,046
For projects with a regular rhythm, you
can plan breaks.

219
00:14:16,096 --> 00:14:19,733
Open the project and go to its Settings
tab.

220
00:14:19,783 --> 00:14:26,287
In the Breaks section, click Add break,
choose a break type and, if you like, a

221
00:14:26,337 --> 00:14:27,926
time and a length.

222
00:14:27,976 --> 00:14:34,890
Here we plan a fifteen minute coffee break
at ten thirty, and an hour for lunch at

223
00:14:34,940 --> 00:14:35,299
twelve.

224
00:14:35,349 --> 00:14:36,528
Click Save changes.

225
00:14:36,578 --> 00:14:42,263
People on this project now see these
breaks as one-tap buttons in the desktop

226
00:14:42,313 --> 00:14:45,950
app, with a reminder when a break is due.

227
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:51,213
Tasks break a project into pieces of work.

228
00:14:51,263 --> 00:14:53,661
Open Tasks and click New task.

229
00:14:53,711 --> 00:15:00,187
Choose the project, give the task a title,
and set its status, priority, due date and

230
00:15:00,237 --> 00:15:01,818
an estimate in hours.

231
00:15:01,868 --> 00:15:04,674
Assign it to one or more people.

232
00:15:04,724 --> 00:15:11,200
When they track time, they can pick the
task, so you see exactly where the hours

233
00:15:11,250 --> 00:15:11,608
went.

234
00:15:11,658 --> 00:15:18,542
Filter the list by project or status, or
switch on Assigned to me to see your own

235
00:15:18,592 --> 00:15:18,950
work.

236
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:27,186
Now let us switch to the worker's side.

237
00:15:27,236 --> 00:15:30,017
Workers use WorkPulse through the desktop
app.

238
00:15:30,067 --> 00:15:34,062
After accepting an invitation, they land
on this download page.

239
00:15:34,112 --> 00:15:39,321
It offers the right installer for their
computer: Windows, macOS, or Ubuntu and

240
00:15:39,371 --> 00:15:39,725
Debian.

241
00:15:39,775 --> 00:15:41,343
Click the download button.

242
00:15:41,393 --> 00:15:47,815
A short guide opens with the install
steps, and a link to the full setup guide

243
00:15:47,865 --> 00:15:50,242
with a picture for each step.

244
00:15:50,292 --> 00:15:55,905
On Windows, for example, if Windows
protects your PC, click More info and then

245
00:15:55,955 --> 00:15:56,714
Run anyway.

246
00:15:56,764 --> 00:15:59,950
The app updates itself automatically from
then on.

247
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:07,950
Open WorkPulse on your computer and sign
in with the same email and password you

248
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:09,150
use for WorkPulse.

249
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:12,750
You can also sign in through your browser
instead.

250
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:16,750
If your organization requires it, an
administrator approves new computers

251
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:18,750
before they can track time.

252
00:16:18,800 --> 00:16:25,150
Once you are signed in, the menu on the
left takes you to everything you need:

253
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:29,150
Home, Track, Timesheet, Time off,
Schedule, Pay stubs and Settings.

254
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:31,950
The app only shows your own data.

255
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:35,156
This is Home.

256
00:16:35,206 --> 00:16:37,567
To start work, choose a project.

257
00:16:37,617 --> 00:16:42,389
The timer starts right away and the status
changes to Clocked in.

258
00:16:42,439 --> 00:16:48,417
You can also choose a task, and change
project at any time with the Change

259
00:16:48,467 --> 00:16:48,819
button.

260
00:16:48,869 --> 00:16:55,249
Below the timer are the breaks planned for
this project, the ones we set up earlier,

261
00:16:55,299 --> 00:16:56,857
ready as one-tap buttons.

262
00:16:56,907 --> 00:17:02,483
Add a short work note so your manager
knows what you are working on.

263
00:17:02,533 --> 00:17:08,511
On the right, Today's summary shows your
tracked time today and this week, how much

264
00:17:08,561 --> 00:17:10,520
was active, and your shift.

265
00:17:10,570 --> 00:17:16,146
If your organization records activity, it
is shown here too, so nothing is hidden

266
00:17:16,196 --> 00:17:16,950
from you.

267
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:22,601
When it is time for a break, tap it.

268
00:17:22,651 --> 00:17:26,658
WorkPulse pauses your time and shows how
long is left.

269
00:17:26,708 --> 00:17:33,554
When a planned break is due, the app
reminds you, and if a break runs long, it

270
00:17:33,604 --> 00:17:36,393
tells you how far over you are.

271
00:17:36,443 --> 00:17:39,639
When you are back, click Clock back in.

272
00:17:39,689 --> 00:17:45,318
If you step away from the computer without
taking a break, WorkPulse notices that

273
00:17:45,368 --> 00:17:48,158
there was no keyboard or mouse activity.

274
00:17:48,208 --> 00:17:52,620
When you return, it asks what to do with
that time.

275
00:17:52,670 --> 00:17:58,299
Keep it if you were working, for example
in a meeting, or discard it.

276
00:17:58,349 --> 00:18:01,950
If you do not answer, your organization's
default applies.

277
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:07,593
At the end of the day, click Clock out.

278
00:18:07,643 --> 00:18:12,450
WorkPulse asks for a short end-of-day
report: what you completed, and whether

279
00:18:12,500 --> 00:18:14,069
the work is finished.

280
00:18:14,119 --> 00:18:17,712
Your manager reads these reports in the
web app.

281
00:18:17,762 --> 00:18:24,188
The report is saved on your computer
first, so it is never lost, even when you

282
00:18:24,238 --> 00:18:24,998
are offline.

283
00:18:25,048 --> 00:18:27,021
Click Submit and clock out.

284
00:18:27,071 --> 00:18:33,093
In fact, if your internet connection drops
at any time, the app keeps tracking and

285
00:18:33,143 --> 00:18:35,926
sends everything when you are back online.

286
00:18:35,976 --> 00:18:37,950
No tracked time is lost.

287
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:41,550
Track holds your work.

288
00:18:41,600 --> 00:18:46,750
Projects lists everything you are assigned
to; click one to start tracking it.

289
00:18:46,800 --> 00:18:52,350
Tasks shows your tasks, and you can start
the timer straight from a task.

290
00:18:52,400 --> 00:18:56,350
Sessions lists the time you tracked over
the last days.

291
00:18:56,400 --> 00:19:01,550
Forgot to start the timer, for example
during a call on your phone?

292
00:19:01,600 --> 00:19:07,150
Click Add manual time, choose the project
and the time, and give a reason.

293
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:12,350
Depending on your organization, manual
time is added straight away or sent to

294
00:19:12,400 --> 00:19:13,950
your manager for approval.

295
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:21,664
Timesheet shows your time for the current
period, with the hours for each day.

296
00:19:21,714 --> 00:19:25,338
Use Previous and Next to look at other
periods.

297
00:19:25,388 --> 00:19:31,460
When the period is complete, click Submit
to send it to your manager for approval.

298
00:19:31,510 --> 00:19:37,583
If your manager asks for changes, the
timesheet comes back to you and the Home

299
00:19:37,633 --> 00:19:40,032
page tells you what needs attention.

300
00:19:40,082 --> 00:19:45,338
Activity shows your own activity blocks
and the apps and websites that were

301
00:19:45,388 --> 00:19:48,195
recorded, exactly what your manager can
see.

302
00:19:48,245 --> 00:19:55,134
Reports gives you your worked hours by day
and by project for this week, last week or

303
00:19:55,184 --> 00:19:55,950
this month.

304
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:03,241
To ask for time off, open Time off and
click Request time off.

305
00:20:03,291 --> 00:20:09,345
Choose the type, the dates, and add a
reason if you like, then click Send

306
00:20:09,395 --> 00:20:09,752
request.

307
00:20:09,802 --> 00:20:14,229
Your manager is notified, and you can
follow the request here.

308
00:20:14,279 --> 00:20:18,299
Schedule shows your working hours for this
week and next.

309
00:20:18,349 --> 00:20:24,403
Pay stubs lists your pay stubs once
payroll is finalized, each one with a PDF

310
00:20:24,453 --> 00:20:25,217
to download.

311
00:20:25,267 --> 00:20:30,915
Finally, Settings shows who you are signed
in as, your organization and this device,

312
00:20:30,965 --> 00:20:32,950
and lets you sign out.

313
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:43,231
Back in the web app, let us see the work
as it happens.

314
00:20:43,281 --> 00:20:45,263
Open Time Tracking, then Live.

315
00:20:45,313 --> 00:20:50,138
Who is working now shows everyone's
status, updated live: working, idle or

316
00:20:50,188 --> 00:20:56,231
paused, or offline, with the project they
are on and how long they have been

317
00:20:56,281 --> 00:20:56,638
working.

318
00:20:56,688 --> 00:20:59,888
Filter by status to focus on one group.

319
00:20:59,938 --> 00:21:05,169
From a member's actions you can open their
activity or their current session.

320
00:21:05,219 --> 00:21:10,044
And if someone forgot to stop their timer,
choose Force stop timer.

321
00:21:10,094 --> 00:21:16,138
The desktop app stops within about a
minute, and the change is recorded in the

322
00:21:16,188 --> 00:21:16,950
audit log.

323
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:24,728
Session history lists every work session:
who, on which project and task, where it

324
00:21:24,778 --> 00:21:29,680
was tracked from, when it started and
ended, and why it ended.

325
00:21:29,730 --> 00:21:32,569
Filter by date or member, or search.

326
00:21:32,619 --> 00:21:38,347
Click a session to see its details: the
time worked, each segment between pauses

327
00:21:38,397 --> 00:21:41,236
and breaks, and every change of state.

328
00:21:41,286 --> 00:21:44,950
From here you can jump to that day's
activity.

329
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:50,550
Activity shows how a day went, in
ten-minute blocks.

330
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:52,950
Choose a member and a day.

331
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:58,950
Each block shows the activity level, the
share of time with keyboard or mouse use,

332
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:02,550
and the screenshots taken, if your policy
records them.

333
00:22:02,600 --> 00:22:04,950
Click a block for its details.

334
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:08,550
Use the activity filter to find quiet
periods quickly.

335
00:22:08,600 --> 00:22:13,750
The Apps and URLs tabs show which
applications and websites were used, and

336
00:22:13,800 --> 00:22:14,950
for how long.

337
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:19,750
Remember: keystrokes are only counted,
never recorded, and members see the same

338
00:22:19,800 --> 00:22:20,950
information about themselves.

339
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:26,642
Remember the report Ava wrote when she
clocked out?

340
00:22:26,692 --> 00:22:29,104
Managers read them under End-of-day
reports.

341
00:22:29,154 --> 00:22:35,258
The summary shows how many reports came
in, from how many people, how many marked

342
00:22:35,308 --> 00:22:38,950
their work as finished, and the time they
cover.

343
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:41,001
Reports are grouped by day.

344
00:22:41,051 --> 00:22:45,104
Click one to read it in full, with its
session.

345
00:22:45,154 --> 00:22:50,847
Previous and Next move through the
reports, and Copy report puts the text on

346
00:22:50,897 --> 00:22:54,950
your clipboard, for example to paste into
a client update.

347
00:22:57,000 --> 00:23:00,236
Monitoring works best when everyone knows
the rules.

348
00:23:00,286 --> 00:23:04,754
Every person can open What is monitored
from their account menu.

349
00:23:04,804 --> 00:23:10,093
It explains in plain language what is
recorded while they track time, which

350
00:23:10,143 --> 00:23:14,611
limits and time rules apply, and who can
see their data.

351
00:23:14,661 --> 00:23:19,539
Owners, administrators and managers are
not tracked unless you choose to track

352
00:23:19,589 --> 00:23:19,950
them.

353
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:28,569
Time entries is where you find and correct
time.

354
00:23:28,619 --> 00:23:34,197
Pick a date range, then filter by member,
client, project or task, or search.

355
00:23:34,247 --> 00:23:39,826
The totals at the bottom show the time
logged, billable time, and the estimated

356
00:23:39,876 --> 00:23:41,032
pay and billing.

357
00:23:41,082 --> 00:23:45,053
To correct an entry, open its actions and
choose Edit.

358
00:23:45,103 --> 00:23:49,476
Change what you need, and give a reason
for the change.

359
00:23:49,526 --> 00:23:55,105
Every change is kept: View history shows
each revision, who made it and why.

360
00:23:55,155 --> 00:24:01,136
You can also split an entry in two,
duplicate it, or select several entries to

361
00:24:01,186 --> 00:24:03,950
mark them billable or delete them
together.

362
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:12,021
Sometimes time needs to be added by hand,
for example a meeting away from the

363
00:24:12,071 --> 00:24:12,426
computer.

364
00:24:12,476 --> 00:24:18,902
Click Add time, choose the member and the
date, and enter either a duration or a

365
00:24:18,952 --> 00:24:20,521
start and end time.

366
00:24:20,571 --> 00:24:25,379
Choose the project and task, describe the
work and give a reason.

367
00:24:25,429 --> 00:24:31,045
Depending on your settings, the time goes
straight onto the timesheet, or it becomes

368
00:24:31,095 --> 00:24:33,474
a manual time request for approval.

369
00:24:33,524 --> 00:24:39,140
Members can also import time from a CSV
file on their timesheet, using the

370
00:24:39,190 --> 00:24:39,950
template provided.

371
00:24:42,000 --> 00:24:45,588
When members submit their timesheets, they
arrive in Approvals.

372
00:24:45,638 --> 00:24:49,631
Click a timesheet to review the days,
projects and totals.

373
00:24:49,681 --> 00:24:52,056
If everything is right, click Approve.

374
00:24:52,106 --> 00:24:57,312
Approved time is final: it is what payroll
pays and what invoices bill.

375
00:24:57,362 --> 00:25:02,163
If something needs fixing, click Request
changes and explain what is wrong.

376
00:25:02,213 --> 00:25:06,205
The timesheet goes back to the member as a
draft.

377
00:25:06,255 --> 00:25:08,227
Reject works the same way.

378
00:25:08,277 --> 00:25:14,290
To approve many at once, use the Approve
button at the top of the list.

379
00:25:14,340 --> 00:25:19,950
Below, manual time requests wait for the
same decision: approve or reject each one.

380
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:28,617
Team week gives you the whole team at a
glance: the hours each member worked on

381
00:25:28,667 --> 00:25:30,700
each day of the week.

382
00:25:30,750 --> 00:25:35,700
It is the quickest way to spot missing
days before you approve.

383
00:25:35,750 --> 00:25:41,533
Move between weeks with the arrows, and
select a row to open that member's

384
00:25:41,583 --> 00:25:41,950
timesheet.

385
00:25:47,000 --> 00:25:48,950
Schedules hold everyone's working hours.

386
00:25:49,000 --> 00:25:53,350
Open Workforce, then Schedules, to see the
week for each member.

387
00:25:53,400 --> 00:25:56,150
To change someone's hours, open their
schedule.

388
00:25:56,200 --> 00:26:02,950
Set the time zone, the date the new hours
start, and the start and end for each

389
00:26:03,000 --> 00:26:03,750
working day.

390
00:26:03,800 --> 00:26:08,950
Saving creates a new version, so past
attendance is still measured against the

391
00:26:09,000 --> 00:26:11,350
hours that applied at the time.

392
00:26:11,400 --> 00:26:14,950
Members see their own schedule in the
desktop app.

393
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:20,582
Attendance compares the schedule with the
time actually tracked.

394
00:26:20,632 --> 00:26:26,634
For each person you see whether they are
present, late, absent, on leave, on a

395
00:26:26,684 --> 00:26:28,652
holiday, or not started yet.

396
00:26:28,702 --> 00:26:35,108
Filter by status to follow up quickly, and
switch between a single day and the whole

397
00:26:35,158 --> 00:26:35,511
week.

398
00:26:35,561 --> 00:26:39,950
WorkPulse can also alert managers about
late starts and missed shifts.

399
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:46,397
Time off requests arrive under Time off,
on the Requests tab.

400
00:26:46,447 --> 00:26:50,439
Here is the request Ava sent from the
desktop app.

401
00:26:50,489 --> 00:26:56,099
Approve it, or reject it with a comment,
and she is notified straight away.

402
00:26:56,149 --> 00:26:59,333
The Calendar shows who is away and when.

403
00:26:59,383 --> 00:27:06,205
On Policies and holidays you set up the
kinds of time off, such as paid time off

404
00:27:06,255 --> 00:27:11,865
or sick leave: whether they are paid,
whether they need approval, and how much

405
00:27:11,915 --> 00:27:13,482
is earned each month.

406
00:27:13,532 --> 00:27:19,546
You can adjust a member's balance by hand,
and add public holidays, which are paid

407
00:27:19,596 --> 00:27:19,950
automatically.

408
00:27:25,000 --> 00:27:27,363
Money in WorkPulse starts with rates.

409
00:27:27,413 --> 00:27:28,972
Open Finance, then Rates.

410
00:27:29,022 --> 00:27:32,591
Bill rates are what you charge clients per
hour.

411
00:27:32,641 --> 00:27:36,211
Pay rates are what you pay members per
hour.

412
00:27:36,261 --> 00:27:41,439
A rate can apply to the whole
organization, a client, a project, a

413
00:27:41,489 --> 00:27:46,667
member, or a member on one project, and
the most specific one wins.

414
00:27:46,717 --> 00:27:52,298
Rates are effective-dated: when a rate
changes, set the date it starts, and past

415
00:27:52,348 --> 00:27:54,309
time keeps its old rate.

416
00:27:54,359 --> 00:28:00,743
Here we give the new Lumen project a bill
rate of one hundred and twenty-five per

417
00:28:00,793 --> 00:28:01,950
hour, from today.

418
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:08,873
Budgets warn you before a project or
client costs more than planned.

419
00:28:08,923 --> 00:28:13,796
Budgets shows how many are healthy, close
to the limit, or exceeded.

420
00:28:13,846 --> 00:28:20,771
Click Set budget, choose a project or a
client, and set the budget in hours or in

421
00:28:20,821 --> 00:28:21,181
money.

422
00:28:21,231 --> 00:28:25,694
It can run for the whole project or reset
every month.

423
00:28:25,744 --> 00:28:30,617
Warn at sets when WorkPulse alerts you,
for example at eighty percent.

424
00:28:30,667 --> 00:28:35,950
The same progress bars appear on the
Overview and in the client portal.

425
00:28:38,000 --> 00:28:43,950
People can submit expenses with a receipt,
such as travel or software, and mark them

426
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:47,550
as billable to the client or to be
reimbursed.

427
00:28:47,600 --> 00:28:52,350
Under Expenses, the Submitted tab holds
the ones waiting for a decision.

428
00:28:52,400 --> 00:28:55,150
Check the receipt, then approve or reject.

429
00:28:55,200 --> 00:28:58,350
Once you have paid someone back, click
Reimburse.

430
00:28:58,400 --> 00:29:02,750
Approved billable expenses can be added to
the client's next invoice.

431
00:29:02,800 --> 00:29:08,350
Like every finance list, Expenses has a
period filter and an Export button for

432
00:29:08,400 --> 00:29:09,950
CSV, Excel or PDF.

433
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:14,362
Invoices turn billable time into money.

434
00:29:14,412 --> 00:29:19,187
The Invoices page shows what is
outstanding, what is overdue, your drafts,

435
00:29:19,237 --> 00:29:21,197
and what has been collected.

436
00:29:21,247 --> 00:29:22,404
Click New invoice.

437
00:29:22,454 --> 00:29:28,837
Choose the client and the period to bill,
and how to group the time: by project,

438
00:29:28,887 --> 00:29:30,043
task or member.

439
00:29:30,093 --> 00:29:34,465
You can include approved billable expenses
and set a tax rate.

440
00:29:34,515 --> 00:29:35,672
Click Preview lines.

441
00:29:35,722 --> 00:29:41,301
WorkPulse builds the lines from the
billable time and the bill rates, and you

442
00:29:41,351 --> 00:29:43,311
can add custom lines too.

443
00:29:43,361 --> 00:29:50,146
Then set the issue date, the due date and
a note, review the totals, and create the

444
00:29:50,196 --> 00:29:50,950
draft invoice.

445
00:29:53,000 --> 00:29:58,950
On the invoice, Download PDF gives you the
finished document with your logo and the

446
00:29:59,000 --> 00:29:59,750
client's details.

447
00:29:59,800 --> 00:30:06,150
Click Send to email it to the client's
contact; if the client has no email, you

448
00:30:06,200 --> 00:30:09,750
can mark it as sent and deliver it
yourself.

449
00:30:09,800 --> 00:30:12,550
When the client pays, click Record
payment.

450
00:30:12,600 --> 00:30:18,550
Enter the amount, the date, the method and
a reference such as the transfer ID.

451
00:30:18,600 --> 00:30:22,550
A payment can also be split across several
open invoices.

452
00:30:22,600 --> 00:30:26,950
The invoice is now paid, and Payments
received lists every payment.

453
00:30:29,000 --> 00:30:31,750
Payroll pays your people from approved
time.

454
00:30:31,800 --> 00:30:36,950
First, pay groups set who is paid
together, how often, and in which

455
00:30:37,000 --> 00:30:37,350
currency.

456
00:30:37,400 --> 00:30:42,950
Then, on the Payrolls tab, click Run
payroll, choose the pay group and the

457
00:30:43,000 --> 00:30:44,950
period, and create a draft.

458
00:30:45,000 --> 00:30:49,350
WorkPulse calculates each person's pay
from their approved hours, overtime and

459
00:30:49,400 --> 00:30:50,550
paid time off.

460
00:30:50,600 --> 00:30:53,350
Each approved hour is paid exactly once.

461
00:30:53,400 --> 00:30:55,750
Add bonuses or deductions with Adjust.

462
00:30:55,800 --> 00:30:58,150
When everything is right, click Finalize.

463
00:30:58,200 --> 00:31:02,150
Finalizing cannot be undone: corrections
go on the next payroll.

464
00:31:02,200 --> 00:31:04,950
Members can now see their pay stubs.

465
00:31:07,000 --> 00:31:09,771
Each member's pay stub is a PDF.

466
00:31:09,821 --> 00:31:14,204
Members also find it in the desktop app,
under Pay stubs.

467
00:31:14,254 --> 00:31:18,234
Once the money has gone out, click Mark as
paid.

468
00:31:18,284 --> 00:31:24,681
The Owed tab answers a different question:
how much do you owe each member for a

469
00:31:24,731 --> 00:31:25,890
period, right now?

470
00:31:25,940 --> 00:31:30,726
It shows tracked and approved time, and
the estimated and approved amounts.

471
00:31:30,776 --> 00:31:33,950
Estimated becomes approved once the
timesheets are approved.

472
00:31:39,000 --> 00:31:42,150
For a quick answer, open Reports, then
Summary.

473
00:31:42,200 --> 00:31:47,750
It shows the time logged, estimated pay,
billable time and estimated billing for a

474
00:31:47,800 --> 00:31:50,950
period, together with average activity and
days off.

475
00:31:51,000 --> 00:31:55,750
Switch between daily, weekly, fortnightly
and monthly periods, and step back with

476
00:31:55,800 --> 00:31:56,550
the arrows.

477
00:31:56,600 --> 00:32:02,950
Below are the hours per day, by client,
and by project, and a table with every

478
00:32:03,000 --> 00:32:03,750
person's totals.

479
00:32:03,800 --> 00:32:08,950
Members who open Summary see only their
own time, and never any money.

480
00:32:11,000 --> 00:32:16,613
The Report library is organized by the
question you want answered: where did time

481
00:32:16,663 --> 00:32:21,871
go, who was late or absent, which
timesheets are still pending, what is

482
00:32:21,921 --> 00:32:23,894
billable per client, and more.

483
00:32:23,944 --> 00:32:27,130
Open a report, for example Time and
activity.

484
00:32:27,180 --> 00:32:33,197
Filter by date, members, teams, projects
or clients, and group the rows by up to

485
00:32:33,247 --> 00:32:36,433
three things, such as member, project and
client.

486
00:32:36,483 --> 00:32:40,074
Export downloads the result as CSV, Excel
or PDF.

487
00:32:40,124 --> 00:32:45,737
Large reports can be prepared in the
background, and you are notified when the

488
00:32:45,787 --> 00:32:46,950
file is ready.

489
00:32:49,000 --> 00:32:52,642
If you need the same report regularly,
save it.

490
00:32:52,692 --> 00:32:55,924
Click Save report and give it a name.

491
00:32:55,974 --> 00:33:02,078
Choose a relative date range, such as last
month, so it always shows fresh numbers,

492
00:33:02,128 --> 00:33:07,412
and share it with everyone who can run the
report if you like.

493
00:33:07,462 --> 00:33:13,976
Switch on Email on a schedule, choose how
often and in which format, and add the

494
00:33:14,026 --> 00:33:14,386
recipients.

495
00:33:14,436 --> 00:33:16,847
WorkPulse now sends the report
automatically.

496
00:33:16,897 --> 00:33:20,950
Saved reports appear at the top of the
Report library.

497
00:33:26,000 --> 00:33:31,728
Settings, Devices lists every computer
signed in to the desktop app: whose it is,

498
00:33:31,778 --> 00:33:35,442
the operating system, the app version and
its status.

499
00:33:35,492 --> 00:33:40,394
From a device's actions you can approve
it, when your organization requires

500
00:33:40,444 --> 00:33:46,998
approval for new computers, ask for a new
sign-in, or revoke it, for example when a

501
00:33:47,048 --> 00:33:48,236
laptop is lost.

502
00:33:48,286 --> 00:33:51,950
A revoked device can no longer send any
data.

503
00:33:54,000 --> 00:33:58,046
Under Security and retention you decide
how people sign in.

504
00:33:58,096 --> 00:34:02,962
Require two-factor authentication for
admins only or for everyone, set how long

505
00:34:03,012 --> 00:34:08,697
a session lasts, require approval for new
devices, and limit sign-in to your office

506
00:34:08,747 --> 00:34:10,745
networks with an IP allowlist.

507
00:34:10,795 --> 00:34:14,842
The data retention settings decide how
long data is kept.

508
00:34:14,892 --> 00:34:20,986
Access review then gives you a regular
check of who can do what: every active

509
00:34:21,036 --> 00:34:25,902
member, who still has no two-factor
sign-in, your roles and their permissions,

510
00:34:25,952 --> 00:34:27,950
and the active API keys.

511
00:34:30,000 --> 00:34:35,992
Screenshots are kept for a set period,
thirty days by default, and older ones are

512
00:34:36,042 --> 00:34:38,006
deleted automatically on a schedule.

513
00:34:38,056 --> 00:34:42,839
Nothing is ever deleted until an
administrator previews what would go and

514
00:34:42,889 --> 00:34:43,644
approves it.

515
00:34:43,694 --> 00:34:48,881
Click Preview cleanup to see how many
screenshots would be deleted, then approve

516
00:34:48,931 --> 00:34:49,686
the cleanup.

517
00:34:49,736 --> 00:34:55,325
If you shorten the period later, the
approval is withdrawn and you are asked

518
00:34:55,375 --> 00:34:55,728
again.

519
00:34:55,778 --> 00:34:58,950
The history below shows every cleanup that
ran.

520
00:35:01,000 --> 00:35:06,231
To connect WorkPulse to other systems,
such as accounting or HR software, create

521
00:35:06,281 --> 00:35:07,450
an API key.

522
00:35:07,500 --> 00:35:13,138
Give it a name, choose exactly what it may
access, and when it expires.

523
00:35:13,188 --> 00:35:17,200
The key is shown only once, so store it
safely.

524
00:35:17,250 --> 00:35:22,075
Webhooks work the other way around:
WorkPulse calls your system when something

525
00:35:22,125 --> 00:35:25,325
happens, for example when a timesheet is
approved.

526
00:35:25,375 --> 00:35:28,575
Add the endpoint address and choose the
events.

527
00:35:28,625 --> 00:35:33,044
You can leave it switched off until your
system is ready.

528
00:35:33,094 --> 00:35:39,544
Each delivery is signed with a secret, so
your system can check it really comes from

529
00:35:39,594 --> 00:35:39,950
WorkPulse.

530
00:35:42,000 --> 00:35:47,292
Finally, the audit log records every
important action: who did what, when, and

531
00:35:47,342 --> 00:35:48,114
to what.

532
00:35:48,164 --> 00:35:51,813
Earlier we deleted a client; here is that
action.

533
00:35:51,863 --> 00:35:58,388
Filter by action, by type, or by date, and
open an entry to see the details.

534
00:35:58,438 --> 00:36:04,553
The log cannot be changed, and you can
export it to CSV for your records.

535
00:36:04,603 --> 00:36:09,895
And for privacy requests, a member's
profile lets you export all of their

536
00:36:09,945 --> 00:36:11,950
personal data, or erase it.

537
00:36:17,000 --> 00:36:23,014
Here is the same organization through the
eyes of Maya, who manages the Design team.

538
00:36:23,064 --> 00:36:26,652
Her Overview shows her team, not the whole
company.

539
00:36:26,702 --> 00:36:32,312
Her menu is shorter: she can approve her
team's timesheets and time off, watch

540
00:36:32,362 --> 00:36:38,780
their work, and manage the projects she is
assigned to, but she does not see rates,

541
00:36:38,830 --> 00:36:40,801
payroll or the organization settings.

542
00:36:40,851 --> 00:36:47,269
That is why two people can see different
menus, and why a page someone else talks

543
00:36:47,319 --> 00:36:49,695
about may be missing for you.

544
00:36:49,745 --> 00:36:54,950
If you need access to something, ask an
administrator to change your role.

545
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:05,977
Let us finish with the questions people
ask most, all answered in the Help Center.

546
00:37:06,027 --> 00:37:09,191
Why are members sent to a download page?

547
00:37:09,241 --> 00:37:12,807
Because workers use the desktop app, not
the website.

548
00:37:12,857 --> 00:37:15,218
Can approved time still be changed?

549
00:37:15,268 --> 00:37:19,236
Yes: reopen the timesheet, correct it and
approve it again.

550
00:37:19,286 --> 00:37:25,664
Once its time is on an invoice, void the
invoice first; once it has been paid,

551
00:37:25,714 --> 00:37:30,084
correct it with a bonus or deduction on
the next payroll.

552
00:37:30,134 --> 00:37:32,896
What happens when a computer is offline?

553
00:37:32,946 --> 00:37:37,718
The app keeps tracking and sends
everything when it is back online.

554
00:37:37,768 --> 00:37:39,325
And are keystrokes recorded?

555
00:37:39,375 --> 00:37:39,727
No.

556
00:37:39,777 --> 00:37:42,539
WorkPulse only counts keyboard and mouse
activity.

557
00:37:42,589 --> 00:37:44,950
It never records what you type.

558
00:37:47,000 --> 00:37:48,958
Troubleshooting covers the usual problems.

559
00:37:49,008 --> 00:37:55,785
A member forgot to stop their timer: force
stop it from Live, then edit or split the

560
00:37:55,835 --> 00:37:57,391
entry in Time entries.

561
00:37:57,441 --> 00:38:03,013
A member's time is missing: check that
their app is online, since offline time

562
00:38:03,063 --> 00:38:07,832
arrives when they reconnect, and that
their computer is approved under Devices.

563
00:38:07,882 --> 00:38:11,848
For time they really did not track, add
manual time.

564
00:38:11,898 --> 00:38:17,470
The Approve button is greyed out: time was
added after the timesheet was submitted,

565
00:38:17,520 --> 00:38:21,485
so click Request changes and approve it
once they resubmit.

566
00:38:21,535 --> 00:38:27,509
And if a member does not have the latest
desktop app: updates download in the

567
00:38:27,559 --> 00:38:33,533
background and install when the member
quits the app from its icon in the system

568
00:38:33,583 --> 00:38:33,934
tray.

569
00:38:33,984 --> 00:38:37,950
Each guide links straight to the page that
fixes it.

570
00:38:43,000 --> 00:38:45,350
Let us recap the whole journey.

571
00:38:45,400 --> 00:38:50,150
You created your organization and set the
rules for time and pay.

572
00:38:50,200 --> 00:38:55,350
You invited your people, organized them
into teams, and set up clients, projects

573
00:38:55,400 --> 00:38:56,150
and tasks.

574
00:38:56,200 --> 00:39:01,350
Workers tracked their time with the
desktop app, with breaks, idle checks and

575
00:39:01,400 --> 00:39:02,150
end-of-day reports.

576
00:39:02,200 --> 00:39:05,750
Managers watched the work, corrected time
and approved timesheets.

577
00:39:05,800 --> 00:39:11,350
And approved time became invoices and
payroll, with reports to tell you how it

578
00:39:11,400 --> 00:39:12,150
all went.

579
00:39:12,200 --> 00:39:14,950
Everything comes together here on the
Overview.

580
00:39:17,000 --> 00:39:18,591
Thank you for watching.

581
00:39:18,641 --> 00:39:23,924
Whenever you need a reminder, open Help
inside WorkPulse: every topic in this

582
00:39:23,974 --> 00:39:29,668
video has a step-by-step guide there, and
the product tour is one click away.

583
00:39:29,718 --> 00:39:31,719
Now it is your turn.

584
00:39:31,769 --> 00:39:32,950
Track, focus, achieve.
